# Dynamic SEO & metadata — production contract

Marketing pages are indexable. The authenticated shell is not. Demo routes
are not. Get this wrong and you ship customer dashboards to Google.

## App Router metadata

- Root `app/layout.tsx` exports `metadata` with `title.default` /
  `title.template` from `publicEnv.appName`.
- Authenticated and demo pages set:

  ```ts
  export const metadata: Metadata = {
    title: "Billing",
    robots: { index: false, follow: false },
  };
  ```

- Use `generateMetadata` when the title depends on params or data
  (`agents/[agentId]`). Await `params`. Return `robots: { index: false }`
  for any session-scoped page.
- Canonical URLs, when added, must use `publicEnv.appUrl` (no trailing
  slash) + pathname. Never use `localhost` in production metadata.
- Open Graph / Twitter: one helper later (`lib/seo.ts` if you add it).
  Do not copy-paste OG fields on every page.
- `app/page.tsx` (landing) is the only page that should be indexed unless
  you add `/pricing` or docs.

## What not to index

- `/dashboard`, `/agents`, `/settings/*`
- `/demo/*`
- `/login`, `/signup`, `/callback`
- `/api/*` (Route Handlers are not documents; still send `Cache-Control:
  no-store` on health)

## When you add sitemap / robots / OG

- `app/sitemap.ts` — only public marketing URLs.
- `app/robots.ts` — disallow `/dashboard`, `/settings`, `/demo`, `/api`.
- OG image route must not render tenant data. No cookies in the image
  generator. If you need a branded OG, use public copy only.
- JSON-LD: `SoftwareApplication` / `Organization` on the landing page
  only. Do not emit JSON-LD from the dashboard.

## Social and share safety

- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` is already set.
- Do not put API keys, org slugs of paying customers, or invoice numbers
  in `<title>` or `og:description`.
- `noindex` is a hint, not a security control. RLS still applies.
